<title>DENMARK: Danish January trade surplus 1.289 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish January trade surplus 1.289 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 1.289 billion crowns in January 1997 compared to a revised 2.294 billion crowns surplus in December, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted the surplus was 2.645 billion crowns in January, compared to 2.946 billion crowns the month before.  </p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     Jan 1997     Dec  1996    Jan 1996</p>
<p>Exports			26.326	 24.281	22.315</p>
<p>Imports			24.841	 21.830	21.095</p>
<p>Trade balance		 1.485	  2.451	 1.220</p>
<p>Trade balance excl ships  1.289	  2.294	 1.075</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted balance excluding ships	     2.645	  2.946	 2.486</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average January trade surplus excluding ships of 2.5 billion crowns. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969652</p>
